katie: quick heads-up — i pulled the docs PR for the troubleshooting / error-ref section into staging and a couple of SDK users reported the snippets don’t match the latest SDK param names. can we triage? :eyes:
sam: which snippet? i ran the curl example from the PR and got a consistent 429 repro on staging (curl returns 429 + Retry-After). pasted minimal output:
```
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Retry-After: 3
{"error":"Rate limit"}
```
sam: i think the root is the example that shows `maxRetries` in the JS snippet — SDK now uses `retryCount` (breaking copy-paste)
nisha: yup — SDK change landed in 2025-11 and we didn’t backport the docs snippet. sg to add a compatibility note. we should include both keys in the snippet and call out preferred one.
mike: also saw confusion about backoff guidance — the docs suggest fixed sleep of 1s, but our best-practice is exponential with jitter. can we replace the naive example with a small helper?
olga: i can draft a compact helper and a short explainer paragraph. proposed function (JS):
```js
async function retryWithBackoff(fn, retries = 3) {
  let attempt = 0;
  while (attempt <= retries) {
    try {
      return await fn();
    } catch (err) {
      if (attempt === retries) throw err;
      const wait = Math.pow(2, attempt) * 100 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 100); // ms
      await new Promise(res => setTimeout(res, wait));
      attempt++;
    }
  }
}
```
nisha: perfect. please keep the snippet language-agnostic note and add the SDK param mapping line: `maxRetries (old) -> retryCount (new)`
katie: plan: olga opens a tiny docs PR that replaces the naive sleep with the helper, adds the compatibility snippet, and updates the error-ref link to the SDK changelog. i’ll review and merge today if green.
mike: also add a short troubleshooting checklist item: "If you see 429s, check SDK param mismatch -> fallback to compatibility key, and respect Retry-After". tiny list is fine.
docbot: docs-ci: PR 7842 staging build succeeded — smoke tests passed (links validated).
sam: can we also add a short migration note for context-window / timeouts? customers copy-paste both code paths; mention `timeoutMs` -> `requestTimeout` rename too.
katie: good catch. olga, can you add that second mapping in the same PR?
olga: yep — will include `timeoutMs (old) -> requestTimeout (new)` and a short note about stream aborts when timeouts happen.
nisha: after merged, SDK team will add a short changelog blurb linking to the docs page. that should close the loop.
mike: sounds good. assigning to katie and olga. :thumbsup:
katie: thanks — will ping here when merged and deployed.
